 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Steady-State Requirement:** The vector field must be fixed (steady-state) for the control volume growth algorithm to work as described. Dynamic fields require time-slicing [S1].
-*   **Temporal Ordering:** If a voxel is visited from a different path, the new propagation time is compared to the existing one. The shorter time replaces the old one to ensure correct temporal ordering [S1].
-*   **Scalar Field Conflict:** Using vector magnitude as the scalar field for color correctly shows speed but prohibits viewing other scalar fields (temperature, pressure). The implementation typically uses a time display instead of dynamic delay to maintain near real-time performance [S1].
